  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 919 AM MST Thu Nov 19 2026\n\nToday and Tonight... \nAnother warm day is in store for today with highs in the low to \nmid 70s. Skies will remain mostly sunny with a few high clouds \nin spots and remain dry as a high pressure system begins to exit \nthe region late tonight.\n\n\nTomorrow through the Weekend... \nOn Friday, an upper-level trough begins to work its way into the \nregion, which will veer dry winds from the west-southwest for most\nof the day. Regardless, highs will still climb into the low 70s \nwith fair weather favored through the afternoon. As the trough \npasses north of the region Friday night into Saturday, winds will \ngradually begin to increase, with the potential for a stray gust \nor two in the lowlands up to 25 mph. Winds will be breezier in \nhigh elevations where wind gusts up to 40 mph will be possible, \nespecially Saturday morning through the early afternoon. \n\nA cold front will pass through Saturday morning, associated with \nthe trough, and will bring cooler temperatures for the area this \nweekend into next week with highs in the low to mid 60s. Any \nchance of precipitation will remain north of the CWA for this \nweekend. High pressure will build back into the area Saturday \nevening through Sunday, allowing for calm winds and fair weather \nSaturday evening into early next week.\n\n\nMonday through Wednesday... \nMonday will be similar to Sunday with fair weather for most of \nthe day and highs in the low 60s. On Monday night, high pressure \nwill begin to exit the area as another trough moves into the \nregion into Tuesday morning. There is a slight chance of \nprecipitation for areas east of the Rio Grande Monday night into \nTuesday, but models disagree with some keeping us dry while others\nshow a low end chance for precipitation. Tuesday afternoon \nthrough Wednesday will remain dry with fair travel weather and \nnear-normal temperatures as we get closer to Thanksgiving.",
